# Lesson Curriculum Indexing

When a lesson is **added, modified, or reordered**, update **all three** locations before finishing.

## 1. Dashboard (`index.html`)

- Update module curriculum cards and drawer lesson lists
- Fix progress counts (e.g. `X / Y Lessons`)
- Add or reorder lesson links with correct number, title, and meta

## 2. Lessons Tray (`assets/lesson-tray.js`)

Add or update the lesson object in the `lessons` array:

```javascript
{ num: "05", path: "lessons/streams-0005-parallel-streams.html", title: "Parallel Streams", meta: "20 min read • Streams API" }
```

Match the module's existing naming pattern (`streams-0005-...`, `oop-0014-...`, etc.).

## 3. Lesson Navigation (`lessons/*.html`)

- Chain `<nav class="lesson-nav">` prev/next links sequentially within the module
- Every nav bar must include: `<a href="../index.html">🏠 Home</a>`
- Update adjacent lessons when inserting in the middle

## Checklist

- [ ] `index.html` drawer and counts updated
- [ ] `lesson-tray.js` entry added or corrected
- [ ] New lesson has Home + prev/next links
- [ ] Neighbor lessons' prev/next links updated
- [ ] Matching `reference/` sheet created when the lesson has one

Full spec: `.cursor/AGENTS.md` → Lesson Curriculum Indexing.
